# FIX-W-1 — Meter converse usage before HOP_BLOCKED throw
# Executed: 2026-07-16T23:30Z | exit 0

## Fix
invoke() now wraps the hop-check in try/catch. On HOP_BLOCKED, it meters
the consumed converse usage (computeCredits + incrementMeter + emitCreditsTelemetry)
before re-throwing. This closes the billing integrity leak where a blocked hop
lost unmetered spend.

## Bonus fix (dormant bug)
AGENT_ROUTING_TOOLS now uses DOMAIN names (hyphens: 'route-to-agent') instead
of wire-encoded names (underscores: 'route_to_agent'). The invoke() path
applies fromWireToolName() before checking isAgentRoutingTool() — the previous
underscore names could never match the decoded tool names. The hop check in
invoke() was structurally unreachable. Fixed by aligning the registry to the
decoded form.

